{
  "dom_id": "step-q117693",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Which of the following expressions gives all of the vertical asymptotes of the function $f(x)=\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}),$ where $x$ is measured in degrees?. Assume that $n$ is an integer.",
  "worked_solution": "The asymptotes of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ are given by the expression\n\n$$\nx={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the asymptotes of $\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(\\frac{x}{4}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{4}={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{4} & ={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={360}^{∘}+n\\cdot {720}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the expression giving all the vertical asymptotes is $x={360}^{∘}+n\\cdot {720}^{∘},$ where $n$ is an integer.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
